course: dictionary
lesson: 701
title: A tree with a very fat trunk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A baobab is a tree you may never have seen, but the words around it tell you a lot. When you meet a new word, look at the words near it, because they are its context. «Baobabs have huge fat trunks that store water and short branches that look like roots.» The clues fat trunks, store water and branches like roots show that a baobab is a kind of tree.
explain: Context can also come from a whole text, not just one sentence. «The baobab stores large amounts of water in its spongy trunk to survive months without rain.» Months without rain and drops its leaves in the dry season tell you why the tree needs a store of water. Ask yourself: what would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: A baobab is a huge tree with a very fat trunk and short branches that look like roots.
fact: Baobabs grow in Africa, Madagascar and Australia.
fact: Baobabs store thousands of litres of water in their spongy trunks, so they can survive long dry seasons.
fact: Some baobabs are over 1000 years old, and some hollow ones have been used as a shop, a prison and even a pub.
fact: They are sometimes called «upside-down trees» because their branches look like roots.
exercise: What is a baobab? | *A huge tree with a very fat trunk | A bird that lives in deserts | A small flower that grows in gardens
exercise: Where do baobabs grow? | *In Africa, Madagascar and Australia | Only in Europe | In the Arctic | In Asia only
exercise: «Baobabs drop their leaves in the dry season.» Why do they do this? | To grow taller | To catch more rain | Because they are cold | *So they do not lose water through their leaves
test: «The baobab stores large amounts of water to survive months without rain.» What does survive mean here? | Fall down in a storm | Turn bright green | Grow new branches | *Stay alive
test: What does spongy most likely mean in «huge spongy trunks»? | Very tall and thin | Hard as a rock | *Soft and full of holes that soak up water | Sweet to taste
exam: Which fact about baobabs is true? | They are small shrubs with thin stems | They have no trunk at all | They live only in the Arctic | *They can live for over a thousand years
